      <div class="case-content">
        <section id="summary">
          <h2>1. The challenge of multi-industry client-side ERP</h2>
          <p>
            Commercial management suites typically degrade along two axes as scope grows: monolithic memory overhead that overwhelms low-cost POS terminals, and UI-only permission checks that leave destructive inventory, cash, or payroll mutations exposed.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Meson</strong> decouples operational governance into five layers: a <strong>44-module deferred registry</strong>, operation-level <strong>RBAC enforcement</strong>, <strong>deterministic native Rust engines</strong> (<code>crates/meson_features</code>), <strong>Atelier HR</strong>, and an <strong>offline-first Device Hub</strong> linked to a centralized cryptographic control plane (<code>apps/meson_central</code>).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="modularity">
          <h2>2. 44-module deferred registry &amp; granular RBAC</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Deferred loading &amp; internal Store (<code>module_registry.dart</code>):</strong> 44 functional modules (POS, Kitchen KDS, Bar, Inventory, Costs, Analytics, Atelier HR, Accounting, etc.) are lazy-loaded via <code>deferred as</code> and gated by active subscription tiers in <code>LicenseNotifier</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Operation-level RBAC (<code>PermissionNotifier</code>, <code>ShellOperationAccess</code>, <code>PermissionWrapper</code>):</strong> maps roles to granular keys (<code>inventory:write</code>, <code>finance:read</code>, <code>settings:manage</code>) enforced inside operation handlers rather than solely hiding UI buttons.</li>
            <li><strong>Multi-tenant isolation (<code>tenant_resolver.dart</code>):</strong> local queries and caches enforce strict tenant scoping (verified by <code>tenant_isolation_test.dart</code> and <code>tenant_isolation_db_test.dart</code>).</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="bom">
          <h2>3. Deterministic BOM, GS1 retail, promotions &amp; KDS CRDT engines</h2>
          <div class="paper-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="en-erp-cap">
            <table class="paper-table">
              <caption id="en-erp-cap">Table 1 · Deterministic operational rules verified in <code>crates/meson_features</code> (78/78 live tests) and <code>meson_models</code></caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Engine / Calculation</th>
                  <th scope="col">Rule / Invariant</th>
                  <th scope="col">Module &amp; verification</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Nested BOM + FEFO/FIFO</th>
                  <td data-label="Rule"><code>Usage = (Base × Mult) ÷ YieldRate</code>, 2–3 node &amp; self-reference cycle detection, depth clamp at 5, concurrent atomic deductions, and FEFO expiry ordering.</td>
                  <td data-label="Module"><code>inventory_core.rs</code> (<code>nested_bom_rust_test</code> 10/10, <code>inventory_concurrency_test</code> 22/22, <code>adversarial</code> 8/8)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Shrinkage &amp; Par-Level</th>
                  <td data-label="Rule"><code>Shrinkage = Expected − (Physical + Usage)</code>; replenishment when <code>Current + Incoming &lt; ParMin</code>; BCG menu engineering &amp; break-even analysis.</td>
                  <td data-label="Module"><code>shrinkage_calculator_logic.dart</code> · <code>finance_engine.rs</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">GS1 / EAN embedded barcodes</th>
                  <td data-label="Rule">Modulo-10 check-digit validation (EAN-8/12/13) and native extraction of <code>plu_code</code>, <code>weight_grams</code>, and <code>price_cents</code> from deli/produce scale barcodes.</td>
                  <td data-label="Module"><code>barcode_engine.rs</code> (4/4 passing unit tests)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Exact retail promotions</th>
                  <td data-label="Rule">Integer-cent <code>u32</code> evaluation selecting the lowest valid line total across <code>Percentage</code>, <code>Fixed</code>, <code>MultiBuy</code>, <code>Bogo</code>, and <code>WholesaleTier</code> rules.</td>
                  <td data-label="Module"><code>retail_promotions.rs</code> (3/3 BOGO/MultiBuy/Wholesale tests)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">KDS CRDT &amp; offline nutrition</th>
                  <td data-label="Rule">Deterministic ticket status precedence CRDT with zero-allocation batch status aggregation plus offline SQLite nutrition lookup (<code>ingredients.db</code>).</td>
                  <td data-label="Module"><code>kitchen_engine.rs</code> (8/8 tests) · <code>nutritional_engine.rs</code></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="hr">
          <h2>4. Atelier HR: attendance kiosk state machine &amp; payroll</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Workforce lifecycle (<code>features/atelier/</code>):</strong> unifies job postings, candidate pipelines, worker profiles (<code>worker_profile/</code>), shift scheduling (<code>turnos_horarios/</code>), contracts, and payroll calculation (<code>nomina/</code>: gross/net pay, deductions, tips, and bonuses).</li>
            <li><strong>Offline attendance kiosk (<code>asistencia_tab.dart</code>):</strong> runs an explicit shift state machine (<code>checked_in</code> → <code>break</code> → <code>checked_out</code> / <code>overtime</code>) with PIN/ID or biometric verification and deferred punch sync.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="licensing">
          <h2>5. Central control plane, HMAC licensing &amp; multi-protocol Device Hub</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Hardware-bound anti-clock licensing (<code>license_engine.rs</code>):</strong> binds node licenses to <code>HardwareFingerprint</code> (via <code>sysinfo</code>) signed with <code>HMAC-SHA256</code> and guarded by <code>ClockDriftDetector</code> against OS clock rollbacks.</li>
            <li><strong>Multi-protocol discovery &amp; offline IoT (<code>services/device_hub/</code>):</strong> <code>DiscoveryService</code> (662 LOC) unifies mDNS (<code>Bonsoir</code>), Bluetooth thermal printers, and a native Rust LAN scanner (<code>device_scanner.rs</code>); <code>IoTService</code> (454 LOC) persists device state per zone in Isar (<code>LocalIoTDevice</code>) for cloud-free control.</li>
            <li><strong>Resilient failover print queue (<code>station_print_queue.dart</code>):</strong> per-station buffer (kitchen, bar, cashier) with retries, automatic <code>StationFailoverRoute</code> rerouting to backup printers, and injectable <code>PrintExecutor</code> for deterministic testing.</li>
            <li><strong>Anti-theft self-checkout, terminals, CFD &amp; WebRTC:</strong> RS-232/USB serial scale weight verification vs. scanned barcodes, <code>TcpPaymentTerminal</code> / <code>SmartPosAndroidTerminal</code> adapters guarded by <code>PendingPaymentApprovalGuard</code>, secondary display streaming (<code>StreamingService</code> / <code>DisplayChannel</code>), and native LAN P2P signaling (<code>crates/meson_webrtc</code> over <code>webrtc 0.17.1</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Super-admin console (<code>apps/meson_central</code>):</strong> aggregates fleet telemetry, cryptographic license issuance, multi-tenant tickets, and SaaS financial metrics.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="validity">
          <h2>6. Live test evidence &amp; explicit operational boundaries</h2>
          <p>
            In November 2026, live execution of <code>cargo test -p meson_features</code> passed <strong>78 / 78 tests (0 failures in 0.32 s)</strong> covering unit tests (26), concurrency &amp; unit-conversion safety (22), adversarial JSON-bomb/FEFO tests (8), PN-Counter CRDT (4), KDS CRDT/state machine (8), and cycle-safe nested BOMs (10). These complement <strong>24 domain test suites</strong> in <code>packages/meson_models/test/</code>, <strong>7 DB suites</strong> in <code>packages/meson_db/test/</code>, and Dart tests for <code>station_print_queue</code>, <code>device_hub</code>, <code>retail_pos</code>, and Atelier inside <code>apps/meson_business/test/</code>.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Explicit boundaries (documented in <code>SUITES_AUDIT_AND_ROADMAP.md</code>):</strong> while MesOn Store lists 18 vertical suites, production-grade logic is concentrated in Restaurant, Retail POS, and Wholesale Marketplace, whereas ~10 secondary verticals (hotel, workshop, clinic, etc.) remain UI façades without vertical domain models; physical RS-232/ESC-POS peripherals and bank terminals require on-site hardware certification.
          </p>
        </section>
